    <string name="g_experimente">Try it:</string>
    <string name="g0_et">Welcome</string>
    <string name="g0_ti">Your cinema, no limits</string>
    <string name="g0_tx">LibertyX opens practically everything — MKV, HEVC, 4K HDR, ASS and PGS subtitles, multiple audio tracks — from your device, a flash drive or your home computer. In one minute you will learn the shortcuts that make the difference.</string>
    <string name="g_no_player">In the player</string>
    <string name="g1_ti">Drag sideways</string>
    <string name="g1_tx">Anywhere on the screen. The exact frame follows your finger instead of jumping from scene to scene, and the bubble shows where you are going and how far you moved.</string>
    <string name="g1_te">drag your finger right or left on the video</string>
    <string name="g1_fe">That is how you find a scene.</string>
    <string name="g2_ti">Brightness on the left, volume on the right</string>
    <string name="g2_tx">Drag up or down. Brightness applies only to the video and goes back to normal when you leave; volume is the device\'s, without the system slider covering the picture.</string>
    <string name="g2_te">slide your finger up or down on each half</string>
    <string name="g2_fe">Both sides, without leaving the movie.</string>
    <string name="g3_ti">Double tap</string>
    <string name="g3_tx">On the right it skips ahead 10 seconds, on the left it goes back 10. In the middle it pauses and resumes. Missed a line? Two taps on the left.</string>
    <string name="g3_te">tap twice quickly on the right, left or middle</string>
    <string name="g3_fe">Skipped without even looking at the buttons.</string>
    <string name="g4_ti">Hold to speed up</string>
    <string name="g4_tx">While your finger stays on the screen, the video runs at 2× — let go and it returns to normal. Great for getting through a slow part. The hold speed is chosen in the three-dot menu, from 1.5× to 4×.</string>
    <string name="g4_te">hold your finger on the video for a moment</string>
    <string name="g4_fe">Let go, back to normal.</string>
    <string name="g5_ti">Pinch to zoom</string>
    <string name="g5_tx">Spread two fingers to get close to a detail, from 0.5× to 6×, and drag with both to move the zoomed picture. “Reset zoom”, in the three-dot menu, brings back the full frame.</string>
    <string name="g5_te">spread two fingers on the video</string>
    <string name="g5_fe">A close-up of the detail.</string>
    <string name="g6_ti">Fine seeking on the bar</string>
    <string name="g6_tx">While dragging the handle on the time bar, move your finger up: the bar starts moving slower — half, a quarter, a tenth. That is how you hit the exact second in a two-hour movie.</string>
    <string name="g6_te">drag the handle and, without letting go, move your finger up</string>
    <string name="g6_fe">Watchmaker precision.</string>
    <string name="g_ferramentas">Tools</string>
    <string name="g7_ti">The island and the menu</string>
    <string name="g7_tx">The island, just below the title, holds what you use during the movie. The three dots in the top corner open the rest. Tap each one to see what it does.</string>
    <string name="g7_te">tap three tools</string>
    <string name="g7_fe">Now you know the toolbox.</string>
    <string name="g8_ti">Everything on your device, already organized</string>
    <string name="g8_tx">Folders become covers, and “Continue watching” remembers where you stopped in each video — when you open it again, the app asks whether to resume. Downloaded something new? Pull the screen down to refresh.</string>
    <string name="g8_te">pull the list down and let go</string>
    <string name="g8_fe">Library refreshed.</string>
    <string name="g_na_rede">On the network</string>
    <string name="g9_ti">Your home computer, in your pocket</string>
    <string name="g9_tx">The servers icon, at the top of the library, finds the computers and NAS on your network with shared folders by itself and plays straight from them, without downloading anything. In the car, Android Auto plays the videos\' audio.\n\nWhen you tap Get started, Android will ask for access to your videos. Nothing leaves the device — the scan is local. To see this guide again: Display › See the guide.</string>
    <string name="g9_te">tap the servers icon</string>
    <string name="g9_fe">This is how you reach your home computer.</string>
    <string name="g_slogan">Your media. Your freedom.</string>
